---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Golden Wings: Stewardess to Sky Queen"
  description="Three generations in American Airlines livery, one 747 that outlived the men who flew it, and a son with an inheritance he can't pass down the usual way."
  path="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Documentary short · ~22 min</span>
      <h1>Golden Wings: Stewardess to Sky Queen</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Three generations in American Airlines livery, one 747 that outlived the men who flew it,
        and a son with an inheritance he can't pass down the usual way.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/watch">Watch</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/press">Press</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="subject-heading">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Subject</span>
      <h2 id="subject-heading"><a href="/people/robyn-stewart">Robyn Stewart</a></h2>
      <p>
        Robyn Stewart has flown for American Airlines since 1971. Mother. Gold Wings. More than
        fifty years in the cabin. This film is about her life in the air and the family that
        worked there with her.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/people/robyn-stewart">Read her page</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tight" aria-labelledby="bridge-heading">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">747</span>
      <h2 id="bridge-heading">The airplane that connects them</h2>
      <p>
        Jay R. Ricks helped build American Airlines' 747 training program. Robyn was among the
        early cabin crew on that airplane. Years later the three of them flew together. That is
        where the film starts: the Golden Age of air travel, on a 747.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="generations-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Family</span>
      <h2 id="generations-heading">In American Airlines livery</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3><a href="/people/jay-r-ricks">Jay R. Ricks</a></h3>
          <p>Flight engineer. 747 training.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3><a href="/people/robyn-stewart">Robyn Stewart</a></h3>
          <p>Gold Wings. American Airlines flight attendant.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Caleb Mills Stewart</h3>
          <p>Director</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3><a href="/people/jock-bethune">Jock Bethune</a></h3>
          <p>On camera. Living witness.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3><a href="/people/millie-alford">Millie Alford</a></h3>
          <p>Stewardess College research.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tight" aria-labelledby="awards-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Proof</span>
      <h2 id="awards-heading">Awards</h2>
      <ul class="awards-strip">
        <li>Best Cinematography · Silicon Beach Film Festival 2024</li>
        <li>Best Documentary Short · Guadalajara, Swedish International, and Clown</li>
        <li>Best Mobile Short · Independent Shorts Awards 2024</li>
        <li>TCL Chinese Theatre premiere</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Programmers and press</h2>
      <p class="muted">Screener, DCP, ProRes, or a direct line.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/press">Press</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
